-     entry .sessional   the given which makes an `Endpoint` `Sessional`, lending a `Session` to a block
-         An `EndpointSessional`, capturing `Online` and the `Tactic[Ssh.Error]` it is built
-         with. In implicit scope through the companion; the contextual values it needs are
-         listed on `Ssh.Endpoint`.
-     entry #host   the host to connect to, as a name or an address
-     entry #port   the TCP port, 22 for a standard server
-     entry #user   the user to authenticate as
-     entry #signers   the proofs of identity to offer, in order; the first the server accepts is used
-     entry #resolved   the endpoint as an `SshConfig` resolves it: its `HostName`, `Port` and `User`
-         `endpoint.resolved(config)` looks `#host` up as a `Host` pattern and replaces the
-         host with the configuration's `HostName`, the port with its `Port`, and the user with
-         its `User` if one is set (keeping the endpoint's own otherwise). The signers are
-         unchanged: an `IdentityFile` is a path the caller must load.
+     entry .sessional   given, делающий `Endpoint` экземпляром `Sessional`, который предоставляет блоку на время `Session`
+         `EndpointSessional`, захватывающий `Online` и `Tactic[Ssh.Error]`, с которыми он
+         построен. Находится в неявной области видимости через компаньон; нужные ему
+         контекстные значения перечислены в `Ssh.Endpoint`.
+     entry #host   хост для подключения, в виде имени или адреса
